    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0201" n="[127]" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg127"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        King.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 18, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received and have read with very
                    great interest your despatch of November 18th, No. 46, in which you give an
                    account of recent interviews between yourself and his Holiness and the cardinal
                    secretary of state. The spirit in which the remarks of his Holiness were
                    conceived cannot be too highly commended, and the sentiments of cordiality and
                    good feeling which were expressed both by him and by his Eminence Cardinal
                    Antonelli towards the government and people of the United States are fully and
                    warmly appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rufus King,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c, &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
